title Caravan carry -- two real processes share one declared region
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, rota doc per lap, send each finished increment.
think Read KYRI and RADIANT_STYLE first, then crux/REMEMBER, the 1024-round itinerary, the eight-season double-seat, the crypto decision wave, and the top three rows of session-logs/README with their recommend lines.
think Standfast pass over crux/REDS.md -- rows 80, 83, 84, 85 are the live ledger and all four carry closures proven on metal. #80's booked count-guard loom stands as tools/crypto_count_guard_witness.rish and is called from crypto_suite_witness. #85 was reopened and honestly closed 20260819.134229. No open agent-closable red, so the line is clear for constructive work.
think The running thread named its own crux twice over -- the newest log recommend and the REMEMBER live edge both ask for a child PROCESS that exercises its granted region across the boot seam, so the carry happens between two real processes rather than two capability lists sharing one address space. That is the Lindy-first crux: exercise.rye proved the policy and could never prove the seam.
think Read boot.rye and exercise.rye whole before writing, so the new ring composes over them rather than restating them -- carry.rye imports boot's argv capability wire (write_cap_word, read_cap_word, line_agrees) and exercise's provisioning and Reach, and adds only what is genuinely new: a plan wire, an outcome vocabulary, and a supervisor that judges.
think Design call -- the child must learn its region's extent without ever reading the declaration, since a child that reads the document is not a child. Took the extent from the provisioned store's own length: the parent sized that store at exactly the declared length and nothing widens it, so a bound settled before the run still holds inside a process that never saw the document. Static allocation is why this works, and that is the seL4 teaching arriving as consequence.
think Design call -- judgment belongs to the supervisor, never to the component. A child attempts one task and reports an exit code from a closed vocabulary (carried 0, malformed 1, NotGranted 3, WriteDenied 4, PastEnd 5, bytes differed 6, all avoiding supervisor_exit.stop_requested at 8); the parent asserts which code it expected. A child that quietly did nothing therefore cannot report success.
think GREEN arrived on the first metal pass, so both RED paths were proven before the green was trusted. Asking the producer to open rx_a without writing left the consumer reading zeros and it answered bytes differed. Letting a child grant itself a capability its argv never carried let client_b reach rx_a, caught by name at exit 1.
think First witness run went RED honestly -- the disk read-back found zeros, because every carry_system call re-provisions and the refusal plan ran last, truncating the store the carry had just filled. Fixed by ordering the self-test refusals-first and carry-last, and by naming the fresh-provisioning property in the module header rather than hiding it: each run opens zeroed, so an arriving byte belongs to this run.
obs Order stopped being tidy and became load-bearing. The carry works precisely because declaration order is startup order -- serial_stack.bron names serial_virt before client_a, so the producer has already exited when the consumer opens the region. A startup sequence written into a document is a real sequence at run time, and that is a property the four rings before this one described without ever depending on.
obs The refusals mean something different across a process seam than they did inside one. In exercise.rye a refusal was a policy answer computed beside the thing it refused; here client_b holds no words for rx_a anywhere in its address space, so the refusal is structural rather than consulted. The RED probe that granted a child more than its argv carried is what makes that claim checkable rather than merely felt.
obs TAME caught a real tidy break -- two compound asserts in the comptime block. Split into four so a failing half names itself.
obs Rota item 25 read this lap -- active-designing/20260816-205859_double-seat-expansion-eight-seasons.md, the eight to-do seasons. It confirms the Microkernel Target sits above the eight as the Lindy-priority double-seat, and that Season G's open-media family and Season H's open weights are the recommended work waiting behind it.
loom witness=caravan_carry_witness processes=6 carried_bytes=36 regions_provisioned=3 declared_bytes=73728 refusals=4
file caravan/carry.rye the ninth Caravan ring -- a plan wire, a closed outcome vocabulary, a supervisor that spawns one child per assignment and holds it to the code it expected, and a child that reaches a region by name alone through the store's own extent
file tools/caravan_carry_witness.rish proves the carry on metal -- 36 bytes crossing rx_a between two processes, four refusals each in their own child, the store still 4096 bytes, every check native contains per the REDS 85 loom
file caravan/README.md the ladder gains its carry row and a Why the Carry Has To Cross a Real Seam section, synced in the same commit as the code it describes
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to the carry ring and the git nib follows it in the work commit
recommend keep-going -- the seam now carries bytes one way, so the next crux is the channel made real: two live children signalling each other over a declared channel, so the notify half of the Microkit shape stands beside the share half. No key, no funds.
